development.question_text:
The function $f(x) = \dfrac{8}{3}(1 - x)$ on $[0,c]$, and $0$ elsewhere, is a probability density function. Find $c$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=4cm, y=1cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- (0,2.667) -- (0.62,1.013) -- (0.62,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.12,0) -- (1.35,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.4) -- (0,3.2) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (0,2.667) -- (1,0);
\draw[thick] (1,0) -- (1.3,0);
\draw (0.62,0) -- (0.62,1.013);
\node[below] at (0.62,0) {$c$};
\node[below] at (1,0) {$1$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A probability density function is $f(x) = k$ for $0 \le x < 2$ and $f(x) = 3k$ for $2 \le x \le 6$, and $0$ elsewhere. Find $k$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.78cm, y=1.2cm]
\draw[->] (-0.7,0) -- (7.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.4) -- (0,2.6) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (-0.6,0) -- (0,0);
\draw[thick] (0,0.6) -- (2,0.6);
\draw[thick] (2,1.8) -- (6,1.8);
\draw[dashed] (0,0.6) -- (0,0);
\draw[dashed] (2,0.6) -- (2,1.8);
\draw[dashed] (6,1.8) -- (6,0);
\draw[thick] (6,0) -- (7.2,0);
\node[left] at (0,0.6) {$k$};
\node[left] at (0,1.8) {$3k$};
\node[below] at (2,0) {$2$};
\node[below] at (6,0) {$6$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

